WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.110
- [Interviewer] Do the
Palestinians have a right

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.160
to a static state?

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.073
- [Netanyahu] No, I
don't think they do. But.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.430
- [Johnny] In 2007, the head
of military intelligence

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.860
for the Israeli army had a meeting

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.590
with the US Ambassador in Tel Aviv.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.420
We're looking at the classified cable

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.120
that summarizes what was
talked about in this meeting.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.590
The topic of discussion was Iran, Syria,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.933
the Gaza Strip and Hamas.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.650
Hamas had just won the
Palestinian elections,

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.710
which kicked off a fight with
the other Palestinian group,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.160
which ended in Hamas taking
over Gaza completely.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.180
They controlled it.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.790
And if you're an Israeli
citizen or the US government,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.890
this is a terrible set of events.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.050
Hamas is a violent extremist group

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.700
known to commit heinous violence

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.650
against civilians in Israel,

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.180
and they were now in power.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.940
They controlled the Gaza Strip
an hour away from Tel Aviv.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.530
But look at this leaked document.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.640
In this leaked cable,

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.500
you see that the Israeli official says

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.710
that Israel would be happy
if Hamas took over Gaza

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.050
because it would mean that
Israel could now treat Gaza

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.760
like a hostile country.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.650
- [Reporter] Three days post cease fire,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.380
and there's unrelenting bombing in Gaza.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.110
- [Johnny] This document
is a view into a strategy

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.510
that right-wing factions
within the Israeli government

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.210
have used for decades in an effort to win

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.510
one of the most divisive
conflicts in the world today,

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:28.590
in which two groups are fighting
over one piece of holy land

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.160
and one side is winning by
using a very specific tactic,

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.980
one that the world says
is illegal and immoral,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.650
and one that worked for a short time,

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.280
but that recently has
been shown to be a recipe

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.433
for even worse violence
and conflict and suffering.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.830
In this video, I wanna lay out
what this strategy looks like

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.120
and show you how it failed.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.210
I know this is a topic that
is full of deep emotions

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.300
that has real stakes in people's lives.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.150
Please know that I am
earnest in my efforts

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.940
to tell this story with
clarity and with accuracy.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.610
And also please note that
this is not a full account

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.370
of the conflict between
Israel and its neighbors,

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.820
but I do hope that it sheds
light on a view of the conflict

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.488
that sometimes gets lost
in all of the yelling.

00:02:14.488 --> 00:02:17.155
(intense music)

00:02:21.965 --> 00:02:25.882
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:27.028 --> 00:02:29.778
(crowd cheering)

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.970
For 2000 years, Jewish
people around the world

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.640
have been persecuted and segregated

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.760
and ostracized from society.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:51.750
That is a fact.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.120
By the time the 1800s came around,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.030
it became clear that
wherever the Jews went,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.713
persecution would follow.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.770
This is when a movement
emerged calling for Jews

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.160
to come together and to create
a country for themselves

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.390
where they could govern themselves

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.360
and be free from all
of this racist hatred.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.820
The creation of a Jewish
country would have

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.710
at the top of its priority list

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.660
the security of the Jewish people.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.890
But the big question was where?

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.930
Several places floated
around in proposals,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.480
Argentina, even modern day Kenya,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.013
which back then was Uganda.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.960
But most people in this
movement wanted the Jews

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.330
to return to their historic homeland,

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.893
a place called Palestine.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.500
Where Jews built their temple

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.900
and their culture 3000 years ago,

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.070
but then were exiled,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.620
and now there was this call to return

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.060
so that Jews could feel safe

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.823
after 18 centuries of Jewish suffering.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.260
So as the 1900s came around,

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.810
tens of thousands of
Jews, mostly from Europe,

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.523
flocked to Palestine,

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.200
which eventually came under
control of the British.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.570
The British were getting
ready to leave this region

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:12.450
and were struggling to
contain the growing conflict

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:16.080
between Native Arabs and
all these Jewish immigrants.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.320
Then in the 1940s came a horrific genocide

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.450
against the Jewish people in Europe,

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.033
led out by Hitler and his Nazi regime.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.860
This created a wave of
international support

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.470
for this idea of giving the Jewish people

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.480
a homeland where they could be safe.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.820
Before they left, the British asked the UN

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.820
to determine what would
replace them in Palestine,

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.650
and the UN decided that Palestine

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.300
would become two new countries,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.720
one for the Jews and one
for the Palestinian Arabs

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.610
that had already been
living in this region.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.380
- [Reporter] The Jewish
state colored light,

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.030
the Arab state dark.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.120
Jaffa to go to the Arabs,
Jerusalem internationalized.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.290
- But as happens when outsiders
draw lines on old land,

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.580
there was a problem here.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.050
Within these borders that were meant

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.090
for the new Jewish country,

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.060
hundreds of thousands of
Palestinian Arabs were living

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.760
who would soon have to leave their homes

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.043
to move to their side of the line.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.090
Okay, wait. I'm gonna pause there.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.730
Because as I said this
is not a full history

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.440
of the Arab-Israeli conflict.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.670
We actually just made a video

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.320
on our new channel Search Party,

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.140
which focuses on what happens next,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.990
the conflict between Israel
and its Arab neighbors.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.790
You can go watch that.
Link's in the description.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.080
It'll give you some useful context.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.080
For now just know that this
led to a horrific conflict.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.930
Jewish militias forced over 700,000 Arabs

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.570
out of their homes turning
them into refugees.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.550
The proposed borders shifted around,

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.200
turned into ceasefire lines,

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.850
and after all was said and done,

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:51.150
the Jewish people did indeed
get their own country,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.473
the state of Israel.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.890
And the two important points
here are that number one,

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.620
the very foundation of the Israeli country

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.510
is for security of the Jewish people

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.120
after nearly 2000 years of persecution.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.080
And number two, the location
they chose to set it up

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.270
was becoming, as a
result of this conflict,

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.323
not much safer than Europe.

00:06:11.323 --> 00:06:14.573
(intense violin music)

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:20.103
That's a tension that
follows this whole story.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.290
Okay, so now let's fast forward to 1967.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.430
Israel has its country

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.770
and they fight a short war
with their Arab neighbors,

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.773
and they win that war and they
take over all of this land.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.770
It's a huge victory for them.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.630
I'm gonna take away the
Sinai Peninsula from here

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:38.190
because they did give that back to Egypt

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.380
as part of a peace deal a few years later.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.080
Israel now controls
important pieces of land

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.003
that enlarge their Jewish country.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.790
Many saw this victory as a sign from God

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.310
that they were actually
entitled to be here.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.650
But once again, Palestinians,

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:58.380
nearly a million of whom had
been kicked out of their homes,

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:01.110
were living here in the West
Bank and the Gaza Strip,

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.670
which Israel now controlled,

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.770
but they weren't really
sure what to do with it.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.500
And it's this territory
that would become the stage

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.500
for the strategy that is
the topic of this video,

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.470
where over time this
land would be sliced up

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.390
with roads and checkpoints,

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.700
walls and other military infrastructure

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.500
that would control the movement

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.573
and lives of the Palestinians.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.560
Soon, even Israeli citizens
would start to move out here

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.560
in large numbers building full on towns

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.840
and further dividing up this territory.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.050
Moving citizens into
occupied territory like this

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.233
is something that the world
has deemed illegal and immoral.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.280
So this occupation starts in 1967

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.170
and it goes on for decades,

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.080
until eventually the
Palestinians living here

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.730
can't handle it anymore and
they start fighting back.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.863
This is known as the first
uprising for Intifada.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.310
It started with boycotts,

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.770
but escalated into mass protests

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.560
where Palestinians of all
ages would throw stones

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.600
and sometimes Molotov cocktails

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.700
at much better equipped Israeli soldiers.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.040
It was Palestinian rage exploding

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.520
against Israeli occupation,
and it went on for years.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:16.920
The Israeli government would
respond by cracking down,

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.350
killing many Palestinians.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.480
Another important thing that
happens around the same time

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.780
down in the occupied Gaza Strip
is that a new movement forms

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.480
promising to fight back
against this occupation

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.370
calling for the destruction of Israel.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.023
The group is called Hamas.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.750
The first Intifada showed
that this wasn't gonna work.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.690
Chopping up Palestinian
land, oppressing them,

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.030
keeping them in this occupation,

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.190
was only going to produce more violence.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.650
It wasn't gonna fulfill Israel's promise

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:49.620
to provide security and
safety for the Jewish people.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.910
They had to switch course.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:54.930
- The security of the Israeli
people will be reconciled

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:57.750
with the hopes of the Palestinian people

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:01.650
and there will be more
security and more hope for all.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.150
- [Johnny] So in the 1990s,

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.070
they start getting
serious about peace talks

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.060
with the Palestinians,

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.860
and they come to this agreement
called the Oslo Accords,

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:11.460
which for the first time establishes

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.440
a Palestinian government authority

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.900
and giving it power to
govern pockets of land

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.280
in the West Bank.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.160
It also gave the
Palestinians some authority

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.050
over almost all of the Gaza Strip,

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:25.000
though there were still
settlements in all of these places.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.860
This was a big deal for this conflict.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.330
Like, both sides were
talking to each other

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.320
and coming to agreements

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.110
that was giving like,
authority to the Palestinians.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.970
But another theme of the story

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:39.270
is that hardliners can use
violence to derail peace.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.170
And that's exactly what happened here.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.600
Right wing Israelis start holding rallies,

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.240
calling their Prime Minister
a traitor and a Nazi

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.310
for giving land to the Palestinians.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.630
Some of these rallies are led

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:54.840
by a now familiar character,
Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.540
- The people of Israel want a real peace

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.640
and real peace means peace with security.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.040
Peace they can trust with
a partner they can trust,

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.690
and they don't feel they have it here.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.820
We want a real peace, not a fake one.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.320
- [Johnny] But the peace talks continue.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:11.940
- With all our neighbors,
a comprehensive peace.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.080
- [Johnny] And shortly after signing

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.230
the second part of this deal
to give Palestinians some land,

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:19.020
the Prime Minister Yitzhak
Rabin is assassinated

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.463
by a far right Israeli.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.730
Hamas conducts bus bombings.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:26.340
And the next year, Benjamin Netanyahu

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.623
is elected as the prime
minister of Israel.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.850
And Netanyahu is a key
figure in this story

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:36.630
because his worldview
embodies a way of thinking

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:39.510
that has taken root in
Israel in recent years.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:42.180
The idea that the only
way to give true security

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.820
to the Jewish people is by
doing whatever is necessary

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:48.210
to stop the Palestinians
from having a state

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.433
anywhere in these borders.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.430
- Look, I'm 28 years old.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.870
I've had to defend my country

00:10:57.870 --> 00:10:59.370
in two wars and in many battles.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:01.950
Nobody wants peace more than Israel.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.710
But the stumbling block
to the road for peace

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.070
is this demand for a PLO state,
which will mean more war,

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:10.260
which will mean more
violence in the Middle East.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:11.700
And I think, I sincerely believe,

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.410
if this demand is abandoned,

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.120
we can have real and genuine peace.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.940
- [Johnny] So that was
Netanyahu. He was a 28-year-old.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.190
But when he becomes the prime minister

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.450
a couple decades later,

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.840
he spends his term
sabotaging the peace accords

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.570
that his predecessor had
worked so hard to create,

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:29.970
claiming that the
occupation of all this land

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:32.700
and its people wasn't actually conquest,

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.910
but rather the key for
security of the Jewish people.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:36.750
They had to do this.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:40.620
Security was the one and only
justification for all of this.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.690
So under his watch settlers continue

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.313
to move into the West Bank.

00:11:46.212 --> 00:11:50.160
We found this leaked video
of Benjamin Netanyahu

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.065
talking to some settlers in the West Bank.

00:11:53.065 --> 00:11:56.640
(several voices speaking)

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.610
The cameraman does turn off
the camera for a moment,

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.420
but then turns it back on moments later.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:06.920
(Netanyahu speaking foreign language)

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:12.030
He is admitting to
sabotaging the peace accords

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:15.240
that the Israeli government had signed

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:17.520
with the Palestinians,

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:18.960
that because he disagreed with them,

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.310
he wanted to sabotage them

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:22.710
because he was so against
a Palestinian state

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:26.250
or any form of Palestinian
autonomy in this land.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:27.810
And then he goes on to explain

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.173
what his real thinking
is on the situation.

00:12:33.229 --> 00:12:37.729
(Netanyahu speaking foreign language)

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:49.050
Netanyahu is a fantastic
politician and statesman,

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:51.570
and he's able to sort of cover
up a lot of these policies

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.640
in the name of security.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:56.220
But here we see what he really thinks

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:58.042
as he's talking to these settlers

00:12:58.042 --> 00:12:59.700
thinking he's not being recorded.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:03.750
So unsurprisingly the
appetite for peace breaks down

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.250
on both sides.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:06.720
Palestinians come to the conclusion

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.850
that the Israelis aren't really serious

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.160
about giving them any kind of autonomy

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.270
in the West Bank or Gaza,

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.430
that their situation will never change.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:18.030
And once again, they rise
up in a second Intifada.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:21.143
This one, much more violent,
much more coordinated.

00:13:21.143 --> 00:13:23.810
(intense music)

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:28.080
Hamas becomes a major
player in the violence

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:30.870
with suicide bombings and attacks.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.990
Israel responds with great
force and during the fighting,

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:37.860
1000 Israelis and 3000
Palestinians are killed.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.650
At this point the Netanyahu
way of seeing the world

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.510
is starting to look a lot better.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.770
Peace talks didn't work.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:45.720
All they did was produce more violence.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.420
And so maybe the only
way to ensure security

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:50.760
is to go back to full blown occupation

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.760
of controlling every
move of the Palestinians

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:55.320
in the West Bank and the Gaza Strip.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:57.060
So at this point the occupation

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.530
gets more and more suffocating,

00:13:58.530 --> 00:13:59.880
more walls, more barriers,

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:02.407
more checkpoints, more settlements.

00:14:02.407 --> 00:14:05.074
(intense music)

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:11.010
Then in 2005 Israel withdraws
from the Gaza Strip,

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:13.890
letting the Palestinian Authority
have total control there.

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.810
They turn their attention entirely

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:18.330
to their historic homeland
of Judea and Samaria,

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:19.680
which is the West Bank.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:21.330
The next year an election is held

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.040
in the Palestinian Authorities

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.350
and the winner surprised the world

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:28.320
and would create a new
chapter for this conflict.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:30.360
The winner of these elections was Hamas.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.130
- [Reporter] This is a
very, very bad result

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.520
for the Palestinians and for Israel.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.290
- [Johnny] The incumbent Palestinian party

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.760
that had lost the election

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:41.130
tried to forcibly hold on to power,

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.440
and soon the two Palestinian parties

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:44.970
were fighting with each other.

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:46.560
And it results in this split

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.690
between the two Palestinian governments.

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:50.130
It turns into violence.

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.300
And when the dust settles,

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.100
there's suddenly a bitter divide

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.410
between these two Palestinian groups,

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.143
Hamas completely taking
over the Gaza Strip.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.790
And this gets us back
to our leaked document

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.050
that we started this video with

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:05.850
where an Israeli official is saying

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:08.850
that they would actually be happy if Hamas

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:10.440
took over the Gaza Strip

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:14.313
because now they can treat
Gaza like a hostile country.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.080
Now that they're not occupying it,

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.110
they're not responsible
for the 2 million civilians

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:22.980
who are living there.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.440
They can impose a blockade
to control anything

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.270
coming in and out of the Gaza Strip,

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:30.390
people, food, medicine,
money, building supplies.

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.480
But there was another
reason why Israel was happy

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:35.760
that Hamas now controlled the Gaza Strip.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.520
The Palestinian government
was now deeply divided,

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.100
Hamas ruling Gaza and
the West Bank being run

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.650
by a more moderate, secular
Palestinian faction.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.920
And crucially neither considered
the other to be legitimate,

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.840
which weakened their ability to negotiate

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.050
for any kind of state,
for any kind of country,

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.300
especially when Hamas still refused

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:57.150
to recognize Israel's right to even exist.

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:59.520
This division played right into the hands

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:00.693
of the Israeli right.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:08.520
And this gets us back
to Benjamin Netanyahu,

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:11.103
that enemy of the earlier peace talks.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.410
He gets elected once again in 2009,

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.840
declaring himself Mr. Security

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:22.110
and promising to provide
safety to Israeli citizens

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:24.390
who are still shaken
from the second Intifada

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:26.850
and are now worried
that Hamas now controls

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.530
the entirety of the Gaza Strip.

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:31.110
Netanyahu's playbook
was already made clear.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:32.220
He had said it point blank.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.720
It's what he had been doing for years.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.210
Sabotaging peace talks that
would give Palestinians

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:37.650
any kind of authority over this land,

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:39.840
and continuing to build settlements,

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.450
while continuing in his
words in that leaked tape

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.170
to hit the Palestinians hard
to make it unbearable for them.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:49.410
A complete assault on the
Palestinian government.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:53.400
Dividing and slowly conquering
the Palestinian people,

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.860
making life hard and desperate for them,

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:58.980
controlling their lives,
watching their every move.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:03.000
And this is where we get to
this paradoxical alignment,

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:07.980
almost alliance between
Benjamin Netanyahu and Hamas,

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.123
the enemy of Israel.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:15.600
As long as Hamas held
control over the Gaza Strip,

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.810
the Palestinian cause would
remain weak and divided.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:21.480
Netanyahu would feel justified in imposing

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:23.880
this crippling blockade of the Gaza Strip,

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.770
which in turn gave Hamas legitimacy

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:27.330
among the people of the Gaza Strip,

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:28.920
showing that their armed struggle

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.290
against Israeli oppression was justified,

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.360
provoking them to launch
rockets into Israel

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.460
to show that they were
actually doing something

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.380
unlike the Palestinian
Authority in the West Bank,

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:39.810
which in turn bolstered
Netanyahu's narrative

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.970
that the Palestinians
actually don't want peace,

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.800
they want violence and
the destruction of Israel.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.420
And the only way for security

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.883
is more occupation, more oppression.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.640
So instead of try to take Hamas out,

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.220
Netanyahu overtly supported them

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:02.640
by approving huge transfers
of untraceable cash

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.940
literally delivered in
suitcases into the Gaza Strip,

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.340
cash that would inevitably
end up in the hands of Hamas

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:09.720
to be used against Israel.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.270
He legitimized Hamas by
negotiating with them,

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:14.400
releasing a thousand Palestinian prisoners

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.897
in exchange for one Israeli.

00:18:15.897 --> 00:18:19.290
- The Israeli soldier held
captive by Palestinian militants

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:22.650
for five years is expected
to be freed within days.

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:26.430
- The more Netanyahu could
keep Hamas in power in Gaza,

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.020
but keep them contained,

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:31.020
the more he could ensure that
Palestinians remain divided.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.030
He could keep peace talks
from ever happening,

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:35.760
which in turn gave him time to continue

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.970
to pursue his expansionist
project in the West Bank.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:41.040
And indeed, since 2009,

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:43.170
when Netanyahu became the Prime Minister,

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:46.683
the number of settlements in
the West Bank has only gone up.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.220
And if you look at this map,

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.740
you can see how these settlements

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:55.560
just weave through and carve up this land,

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:57.690
making it impossible to even fathom

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.460
what a Palestinian state could look like,

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.643
which is precisely the
point of the strategy.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.940
I actually reported out here,

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.070
visiting the settlements
back when I was at Vox.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:12.840
I did a series talking to the settlers,

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.430
trying to understand
why they live out there,

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:16.380
what it's like to live
in these settlements

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:19.590
that are strangely peaceful and banal

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.020
and just mundane, people
living their lives,

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:24.570
because they're protected by the army.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:25.980
If you want a deeper dive on settlements,

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.510
you can go watch that series.

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:29.940
But if you're Netanyahu
over the last 16 years,

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.410
you think your plan is working.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.690
Like, you see all these
settlements going up,

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.700
the international community
can't do anything about it.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:36.810
They keep supporting you.

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:39.360
Every once in a while there's
some flare up in the West Bank

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.990
where Palestinians get into a
fight with Israeli soldiers,

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.550
but it gets contained.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:47.340
Every few years Hamas fires some rockets,

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:50.047
which then gives Israel the
excuse to go, as they put it,

00:19:50.047 --> 00:19:53.670
"cut the grass" by
conducting a short, swift,

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:57.090
violent military campaign
to keep Hamas at bay.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.470
And every day that goes by,

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:00.030
the notion of a Palestinian state

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.923
becomes less and less feasible.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:07.200
This is one reason why a
far right Israeli lawmaker

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.230
called Hamas "an asset."

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:11.550
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:14.040
So divide and conquer has
been the name of the game

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.300
in Israel for a long time,

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:18.300
but especially in the last
16 years under Netanyahu.

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:21.960
And again, to the people in
charge, they think it's working.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:25.560
Maybe this violent status
quo, this equilibrium can hold

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:27.480
and the far right can get
exactly what they want.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.010
Security for the Jewish people

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:31.470
and expansion into all of this land.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:35.220
And maybe the occupation will
break the Palestinian spirit

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:37.770
and they would give up on
their dream of having a state.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.050
But that's not what happened.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.420
On October 7th, 2023,

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:46.410
we saw how wrongheaded this
theory of security was.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.570
- In an unprecedented surprise attack,

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:50.640
the militant Hamas rulers of Gaza

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:54.780
sent dozens of fighters into
Israel by land, sea, and air.

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:56.940
- This deadly attack launched by Hamas

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.610
showed us that while Netanyahu's strategy

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.620
of divide and conquer might be good

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.180
for taking over more land,

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.160
what it's not good for is making good

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:07.890
on the original promise of Israel,

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:10.980
which is ensuring the
security of the Jewish people.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:15.233
In fact, his strategy has
produced exactly the opposite.

00:21:15.233 --> 00:21:19.431
(crowd chanting in foreign language)

00:21:19.431 --> 00:21:22.530
Now, the responsibility for
what happened on October 7th

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:25.950
lies with the people who
committed those acts of terror,

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.230
Hamas fighters and their leaders.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:31.680
There is no excuse or
justification for their actions.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.690
But the point I'm trying
to make with this video

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.310
is that there's also others

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:36.750
that need to stand accountable here.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.270
Those who used Hamas as a pawn

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:42.270
to continue this divide
and conquer policy,

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:44.010
who are now engaged in a campaign

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:46.500
of mass bloodshed on civilians,

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:48.720
they deserve to stand accountable as well,

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.370
to the Israeli people

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.800
and to the countries that support Israel.

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:55.290
I believe in the need
for a Jewish state. I do.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:57.270
I think that's a very reasonable proposal

00:21:57.270 --> 00:22:00.420
that Jewish people should feel
safe somewhere in this world.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.960
And yet what we're looking at isn't it.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:05.280
The Israeli project,

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:08.340
the way that it's been
wielded in its current form,

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:10.530
produces the exact opposite

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:12.540
of security for the Jewish people.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:13.373
Thanks for watching,

00:22:13.373 --> 00:22:15.900
